/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_LUTSampling Sampling
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_LUT
 * @brief Sample lookup tables with closed and periodic boundary behavior.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSampling_Goal Goal
 * Compare a closed one-dimensional lookup with a wrapped periodic phase, then
 * evaluate bilinear and trilinear centers in two- and three-dimensional tables.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSampling_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_LUT_Sampling_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSampling_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * Closed coordinate=0.5: value=15; expected=15
 * Periodic phase=0.5: value=20; expected=20
 * Periodic phase=-0.125: seam value=15; expected=15
 * Bilinear center: value=3; expected=3
 * Trilinear center: value=7; expected=7
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * The negative phase is the useful seam case: periodic lookup wraps it instead
 * of clamping it, which is appropriate for oscillator tables.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSampling_Code Implementation
 * \include LUT/Sampling/Shared.cpp
 */
